      "evidence_id": "tei:title",
      "source": "grobid_tei",
      "field": "title",
      "raw_text": "Refined TFHE Leveled Homomorphic Evaluation and Its Application"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "tei:year",
      "source": "grobid_tei",
      "field": "year",
      "raw_text": "2025"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "tei:abstract",
      "source": "grobid_tei",
      "field": "abstract",
      "raw_text": "TFHE is a fully homomorphic encryption scheme over the torus that supports fast bootstrapping. Its primary evaluation mechanism is based on gate bootstrapping and programmable bootstrapping (PBS), which computes functions while simultaneously refreshing noise. PBS-based evaluation is user-friendly and efficient for small circuits; however, the number of bootstrapping operations increases exponentially with the circuit depth. To address the challenge of efficiently evaluating large-scale circuits, Chillotti et al. introduced a leveled homomorphic evaluation (LHE) mode at Asiacrypt 2017."
    },
